==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|reach|id=riichi}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ja|立直|tr=rīchi}}, from {{der|en|zh|立直|tr=lìzhí}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹiːt͡ʃi/|/ɹiːt͡ʃ/<a:sometimes>}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːtʃi|s=2}}
* {{homophones|en|reachy}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|Japanese|_|mahjong}} A [[yaku]] {{gloss|scoring condition}} and 1000-point [[bet]] made by declaring the {{l|en|hand|id=card games}} to be ready, [[wait for|waiting for]] one more {{l|en|tile|id=games}} to win.
# {{lb|en|Japanese|_|mahjong}} A [[call]] for such a bet.
# {{senseid|en|riichi mahjong}}{{lb|en|mahjong|informal|often capitalized}} {{clipping of|en|riichi mahjong}}
#: {{syn|en|[[Japanese]] [[mahjong]]}}
# {{lb|en|[[pachinko]]|often spelled "[[reach#English: riichi|reach]]"}} Being one symbol away from getting a jackpot, usually triggering an animation before the final symbol is revealed.

